# tests/TEST_BUDGET.baseline — the committed collected-test-count ratchet.
#
# THIS IS THE CANONICAL HOME of the test-suite size budget. It is read by
# scripts/gates/test_budget.sh and by nothing else. Same discipline as
# FROZEN_SURFACE / REMOVED_SURFACE in scripts/gates/source_invariants.py:
# edit it HERE (and nowhere else), in the SAME COMMIT that legitimately adds
# tests, with a one-line justification appended to the history below.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# The suite went 1393 -> 2510 collected in ~3 weeks: `def test_` +131%,
# parametrize decorators 29 -> 76, files 37 -> 60. An earlier consolidation had
# already cut it to 977 once and it regrew anyway, so a one-off cut demonstrably
# does not hold. The pre-existing `unit.max_test_file_ratio` gate counted FILES,
# not tests -- 27 files can hold 3000 tests and it stays green -- and it went RED
# on 2026-09-02 and was ignored for 20 days while the suite doubled. This file
# gates the number that actually grew, and turns invisible drift into a
# reviewable one-line diff.
#
# How to change it
# ----------------
#   DOWN: automatic. When the collected count falls more than the allowance
#         below this number, the gate rewrites this file and fails once, telling
#         you to commit it. That locks the reduction in: a later regrowth back
#         to the old number can no longer hide.
#   UP:   manual, deliberate, reviewable. Edit the number below and append a
#         history line saying which RFC/task earned the extra tests. A reviewer
#         sees a +N line in the diff and can ask "could these have been
#         parametrized into an existing case instead?" -- which is exactly the
#         question nobody got to ask between 1393 and 2510.
#
# Never raise this number to make a red gate green without that justification.
# Thresholds (the allowance itself) live in agents/governance/verify-gates.yaml
# and are amendable only via RFC.
#
# History (newest last)
# ---------------------
# 2026-09-23  941  ICR-97 test-budget work: suite consolidated 2510 -> 941 in
#                  27 files (927 at the start of the consolidation wave, +14
#                  contract tests added by the parallel contract-gate fixes).
#                  Initial baseline, measured with
#                  `uv run pytest --collect-only -q`.
# 2026-09-24  961  ICR-97 PR #24 review remediation: +20. Re-measured on this
#                  tree with `uv run pytest --collect-only -q`. The delta is
#                  NOT new cases from this
#                  PR's review fixes -- those reused existing cases. The file
#                  count moved 27 -> 28 (tests/test_quarantine.py, RFC-049
#                  D2-C), which accounts for part of it. The rest is the
#                  gap between the count recorded when the 941 line was written
#                  and the count the suite actually collects; the PR body's
#                  "923" was a third, earlier measurement. 961 is the measured
#                  truth and supersedes both stale figures.
# 2026-09-24  952  ICR-97 /test-budget safe-floor pass: -9 net. Collapsed 3
#                  parametrize tables, deleted/merged 2 duplicate tautology
#                  tests, folded tests/test_registry_backfill.py into
#                  tests/test_registry.py (-2 exact duplicates). 28 -> 27
#                  files. Measured with `uv run pytest --collect-only -q`.
# 2026-09-24  942  ICR-97 RFC-051 D1: -10. Deleted scripts/ocr_spike_eval.py
#                  (sole consumer of the ocr-spike compose profile and its
#                  three services) together with its 10 tests in
#                  tests/test_ocr_fallback.py. Measured with
#                  `pytest --collect-only -q`.
942
